# vLLM saturation watch (#21 headroom visibility) -- FOR THE MODELS HOST
# (ai1), NOT the app host. Samples the vLLM /metrics surface every minute
# (num_requests_running / num_requests_waiting / kv_cache_usage_perc /
# num_preemptions_total / TTFT-p95-over-delta) and pages over ntfy when the
# box is saturating: a queue >4 sustained for 3 samples, KV cache >0.90, or
# ANY preemption increase (the headroom-unsafe signal that must hold the
# ~100K budget raise). Alert-only; it never restarts anything.
#
# INSTALL (operator, on ai1 -- three steps, from the app host; export
# LEGBA_GPU_HOST=<your models-host address> first — this file tracks no real
# hostname):
#   scp /usr/local/deployments/active/legba/scripts/host_ai1_saturation_watch.sh \
#       "${LEGBA_GPU_HOST:?set in host env}:/usr/local/bin/host_ai1_saturation_watch.sh"
#   ssh "${LEGBA_GPU_HOST:?set in host env}" chmod 0755 /usr/local/bin/host_ai1_saturation_watch.sh
#   scp /usr/local/deployments/active/legba/deploy/cron.d/ai1-vllm-saturation-watch \
#       "${LEGBA_GPU_HOST:?set in host env}:/etc/cron.d/ai1-vllm-saturation-watch"
# then make sure pages have somewhere to go:
#   echo 'NTFY_URL=<the legba-alerts topic url reachable FROM ai1>' \
#       >> /etc/vllm-saturation.env        (on ai1)
# NOTE 2026-08-15: /etc/vllm-watchdog.env on ai1 carries NO NTFY_URL today, so
# the existing vllm watchdog's pages are silent no-ops. Without this step the
# saturation watch degrades to log-only the same way (/var/log/vllm_saturation.log).
#
# Disable during maintenance (on ai1): touch /etc/vllm-saturation.disabled
# Verify it is actually running (on ai1):
#   stat -c %y /tmp/vllm_saturation.healthy
#   tail /var/log/vllm_saturation.log
#
# Every minute is deliberate: the page conditions are streak- and delta-based,
# so the sampling interval IS the detection resolution -- at */5 a "3
# consecutive samples" queue alarm needs 15 minutes of sustained saturation
# to fire, which is too slow to catch a budget-raise experiment going wrong.
# Each tick is one docker exec + one localhost curl; the healthy path writes
# one log line and one stamp.
#
# The path below is ABSOLUTE and so is every path inside the script. A relative
# path here is how scripts/loop_healthcheck.sh failed 7,834 out of 7,834 runs
# over 54 days without executing one line of its body: cron runs from $HOME.

SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin

* * * * * root /usr/local/bin/host_ai1_saturation_watch.sh
